lines+=['','Calibration: ζm24 κ=1 has dimJ17, δ=2.956529432>2, N_A(2)−dimJ=−1. The eliminated block contributes16 negatives, rather than17; S contributes0. The actual formula16+0−17=−1 holds. At m120 κ=1 the analogous deficit is also−1, while the primary quarter defect is11 with δ≈5.9e−6. Small δ alone does not remove the extra below-threshold complement levels.','','The ζ pair111.0295355/111.8746592 enters the strict cut at m65 for c=1/4 (both in the same integer step), m55 for c=1/2 (both in the same step), and m77/m78 for κ=1. pair_111_entry.csv includes the nearby same-m halfspacing sensitivity runs. EDGE_ZERO uses exactly half mean spacing π/log(γ/(2π)), not the full mean. all_included_zero_gaps.csv reports every included distinct-height nearest gap, with the requested threshold0.3 flag.','','At ζm24 quarter and half, the closest included gap is unchanged while σ differs by≈1.97e5. At m120 the corresponding σ values differ by≈1.38e17. Quarter2σ²/λr falls from≈.0367172 at m24 to1.76491e−7 at80 and7.39432e−12 at120. A global minimum-gap statistic does not encode the interpolation geometry. CARD_CONDITIONING.md gives this limited hypothesis, its falsifier and the analytic object to hand off.','','paired_planted_index.csv compares each identical-window/identical-cutoff ζ and planted row. The finite observed count defect changes by+1, while N_A(2) changes−1 and dimJ changes−2; final totals are in summary.json. CARD_PLANTED_RELATIVE_INDEX.md states the falsifier and the limited scope. This does not make the true-world baseline defect zero.','','The planted quarter σ at m120 is9.8497447e−15, compared with ζ9.9393158e−15; similar raw capacity is compatible with an indefinite added quartet. Same-κ DH has a different zero density and sometimes J=0: tall E is retained explicitly. The four supplied off-line quartets below230 and their two raw real conditions are all included when belowT. This comparison does not quietly replace DH by a density-matched world.','','The remaining40 original tall-half blanks m80..119 were scheduled for the same MP200/240 method after its cheap120 pilot. Final method/status counts above and tall_acceptance.json state actual completion, agreement gates and diffuse/localized weak-coordinate checks; no A/eigenproblem or E/J/Schur data were changed.','','The single tall-DH120half priority resolved σ≈1.24404677e−66 (q129>d121, J=0) in14.95CPU s. MP200/240 agree for the SAME frozen≈80-digit numerical zero inputs; this does not improve root accuracy or propagate root uncertainty. The rough80−66≈14-digit margin is not an enclosure. Its many receipt digits refer only to that fixed-decimal matrix. No inverse-F formula is used in the tall case.','','Selected MP120 full-SVD replays agree with MP80 weak conditioning to5.37e−66 relative (DHm24quarter),4.78e−67 (ζm80quarter),3.11e−65 (ζm120quarter). Residuals and precision are in validation_120.json. The faster row-frame QR projectors differ from directly formed MP projectors by at most1.67e−15 on the selected checks. These are numerical consistency checks, not outward-rounded certificates.','',f"Across {S['all_rows']} complete-cut/sensitivity rows: {S['Schur_identity_status_counts']}. Maximum saved EQ residual {S['max_E_kernel_residual']:.4g}; maximum frame orthogonality residual {S['max_frame_orthogonality']:.4g}. Threshold-sign/radius guards remain in every row; a numerical pass is not an interval assertion.",'','adaptive_kappa_sectors.csv derives the rank sectors at signed thresholds m⁻² and m⁻⁴ from the same saved spectrum, with strict-cutoff endpoint conventions and unresolved count flags. It introduces no further eigenproblem. Full D/B/G/S and Q/U arrays are retained at selected cells, and every source matrix has its own metadata/hash in matrices/.','','Replay: python3 scan.py --world zeta --m 16 24 80 120 --skip-existing (analogously dh/plant); python3 aggregate.py; python3 report.py. Checkpoint writes are atomic and skip checks validate parsing, identity and the matrix SHA. Environment/session interruption was recovered by resuming only missing cells. No prior A audit or route state was changed.']
